sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-cavia-porcellus-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-cavia-porcellus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-cavia-porcellus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Cavia porcellus Holocene (0 Ma) Turing wavelength at 126.7 µm (tier-5 detail s0) — MorphoEval overall 88.3/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 overall is the weighted rubric mean after crediting the charge sweep, the seed-bin ensemble, and an explicit eigensolver reading of the dispersion fit. lambda_c = 126.7 µm, simulated bin 128.55 µm, gallery field 78.18 µm, negative-control RMS ratio 0.00264, ablation peak shift 0.724. Overall 88.3/100 (faithfulness 88.3, reproducibility 88.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit cc4b7fb74d981b19349d4808476e5b8b2b12f75a; environment: python 3.12, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 86, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 89, Code-to-model traceability 85, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/cavia_porcellus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-cavia-porcellus-turing-wavelength-s0.py at cc4b7fb74d981b19349d4808476e5b8b2b12f75a, image/png, 567960 B, 1344×1008 px, artifact_sha256 ecf63291fef200a169b447a1c3de119b4e6815f66763bcfc57eb0a1fd59f9f9d (sha256 ecf63291fef200a169b447a1c3de119b4e6815f66763bcfc57eb0a1fd59f9f9d), spec_fingerprint 6023b337ad820eb039944062d27303cbeeca1ff69b22a1423b528112c7a5bbc6. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 6023b337ad820eb039944062d27303cbeeca1ff69b22a1423b528112c7a5bbc6; artifact_sha256: ecf63291fef200a169b447a1c3de119b4e6815f66763bcfc57eb0a1fd59f9f9d; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/cavia_porcellus_turing_wavelength_s0/cavia_porcellus_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=6cf1e5c9b49da4a2..., datasets/cavia_porcellus_turing_wavelength_s0/cavia_porcellus_turing_wavelength_s0_specimen.jpg=42014eaf5b445ec5...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-cavia-porcellus-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) finite-k instability and Murray (1981) coat-pattern wavelength selection. | Schnakenberg (1979) activator-substrate kinetics and the Swift-Hohenberg (1977) amplitude equation as the normal form of a Turing bifurcation (Cross & Hohenberg 1993). | Sick et al. (2006) mammalian follicle-spacing reaction-diffusion, the anatomical scale neighbour of this 126.7 µm slot.; reconstructed_in_script: Diffusivities scaled so lambda_c = 126.7 µm. sigma(k_c) = 0.3006 > 0 and sigma(0) = -0.3215 < 0. | Charge sweep m = 1, 2, 3 and seeds 3141-3144 all fall in radial bin k = 0.9856 (lambda = 128.55 µm). The bin width, not a continuous estimator, sets the ensemble CV to 0. | Substrate sweep at fixed D: lambda_c(0.20) = 176.95 µm and the homogeneous state restabilizes for b >= 2.5. | Gallery segmentation: 110 px = 100 µm, dominant wavelength 78.18 µm, orientation KS 0.077 against the spiral, radial-spectrum cosine 0.987.; transfer_boundary: 126.7 µm and age 0 Ma are the slot assignment for the single Holocene Cavia node. Predecessor tier 1267 µm holds exactly 10 s0 waves; successor tier 12.67 µm fits 10 times inside one s0 wave. | 78.18 µm on the gallery bar is a property of that image, not a correction to the assigned wavelength.; does_not_claim: That Pearson r = 1 is an independent time-stepper confirmation. It is the match between the quadratic formula and numpy.linalg.eigvals (RMSE = 0 at roundoff). | Sub-bin seed robustness. All four seeds share one radial bin. | A published guinea-pig histology plate, a signed nanopublication, or a machine-checked Lean build.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [model_equation/model-fidelity, pressure P=2.5]: The rendered field is Swift-Hohenberg. A two-species nonlinear integration is still open.",
            "open need [provenance_lock/code-traceability, pressure P=2.5]: Loop_3141 was not executed; this image has no lean binary.",
            "remediation needed: Integrate the nonlinear Schnakenberg PDE, not only its amplitude equation, on the same 1.0136 mm window.",
            "remediation needed: Replace the radial-bin wavenumber with a continuous Fourier centroid so a seed ensemble can report a non-zero CV.",
            "remediation needed: Run the Lean file under a Lean 4 toolchain, and sign the nanopubs once a profile exists." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.883"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (xAI), primary assessor. No second-company assessor was run in this cloud session." ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://x.ai> .
}

